      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Code Simplicity \u0026 Control Flow:** This is a multi-way branch block with split error paths that duplicate the `!copy.readable || !matched.has_value()` check.\n\nThe old loosely ordered code caused `fp_read_match_secret` to accidentally return `EC_RES_TIMEOUT` on an unreadable secret (because `deadline` was `0`, making `now \u003e\u003d 0` true). Rather than preserving that bug via complex `expected_fgr` gating, we can simplify this block to check readability first, resolving both the duplicated logic and the spurious timeout error code:\n\n```cpp\n\t\tif (!copy.readable || !matched.has_value()) {\n\t\t\treturn std::unexpected(EC_RES_ACCESS_DENIED);\n\t\t}\n\t\tif (now \u003e\u003d\n\t\t    FpTimestamp{ FpClock::duration{ copy.deadline.val } }) {\n\t\t\treturn std::unexpected(EC_RES_TIMEOUT);\n\t\t}\n\t\tif (expected_fgr.has_value() \u0026\u0026 *matched !\u003d *expected_fgr) {\n\t\t\treturn std::unexpected(EC_RES_ACCESS_DENIED);\n\t\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/d02eb2ee-a60a-4539-bf81-8656191e4735)",
